# painting.
#
# On the Jolla Phone 2 (Mali-G610) with GPU tile painting, root-layer tiles show
# black mid-fling while the page is still loading (Wikimedia Commons: black in
# 3 of 6 cold runs, 0 of 6 once every image had loaded; never with CPU
# painting). The compositor-side tile grid is intact, so the tiles exist but
# their textures hold no painted content. Suspect: a PARTIAL update (dirty
# sub-rect only) landing on a texture whose previous contents were just
# discarded -- freshly acquired because the tile had none or a low-res one of
# another size, reset on an alpha flip, or dropped by a tile-rect change.
# Only the dirty rect is then written and the rest of the tile shows whatever
# the pool texture held.
#
# Logs, to the WebProcess stderr:
#   [tilereset] gpu|cpu partial reason=no-texture|size|alpha rect_reset=0|1 was_lowres=0|1 src=... tile=...
#   [tilereset] skip-no-texture tiles=N of M   (tiles skipped at composite for lack of a texture)
# Nothing is logged, and nothing changes, when the variable is unset.
